     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Most guidelines cap the usual dose at 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCan you check whether one of these was intended?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day, a common target dose)\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1700 mg per day, divided** (for example, 850 mg twice daily)\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and give me the clinical reason. I can enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
